    "lawCode": "Add §336, County L; amd §186-g, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "County Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5698A\n\nSPONSOR: MAY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the county law and the tax law, in\nrelation to communications service surcharges applied to Madison county;\nand providing for the repeal of such provisions upon expiration thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis legislation grants the authorization for Madison County to charge a\n$.65 per access line per month wireline communication service surcharge\nto fund an enhanced 911 (E911) emergency telephone system for the coun-\nty.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends the county law by adding a new section 336, which\npermits the county of Madison to establish a surcharge not to exceed\nsixty-five cents per access line per month on the customers of, every\nservice supplier within the municipality to pay for the costs associated\nwith the adoption of an enhanced 911 emergency telephone system for the\ncounty. It also requires any local law to state, to the extent practica-\nble, the date on which such E911 service is to begin. Such local law may\nauthorize the service supplier to begin billing its customers for such\nsurcharge prior to the date the E911 system service is to begin.\n\nSection 2 amends the tax law to authorize Madison County to impose an\nadditional monthly wireless surcharge.\n\nSection 3 effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIn 2009, the NYS Legislature gave Onondaga County the authority to\ncharge a $.65 per access line per month wireline communication\nsurcharge. This funding stream was used to fund the building of the\nOnondaga County Interoperable Communications System (OCICS). The OCICS\nprovides a single interoperable communications platform that supports\nmore than 160 village, town, county, state, federal and tribal public\nsafety agencies in Onondaga County. Additionally, Onondaga County main-\ntains and shares the OCICS system with Cayuga, Jefferson, Madison, Onei-\nda and Oswego counties in the Central NY Interoperable Communications\nConsortium helping to support public safety and public service radios\nacross the region.\n\nThe OCICS has been a resounding success in helping first responders\nacross the region communicate. Madison County is seeking a similar\nauthority in order to enact similar policies. The surcharge would gener-\nate money for Madison County to help maintain and upgrade the OCICS\nsystem. Additionally, it will help the County with future maintenance\nand upgrade and with the implementation of its next generation 9-1-1\ntechnology. Giving Madison County the authority to implement this\nsurcharge is important to protecting public safety in Madison County and\nCentral NY.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately, with the provision that the act shall expire and be deemed\nrepealed ten years after enactment.\n",
